{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Mi-saḥ.</b> The dagesh in the samekh is because of the assimilation of the nun. The word is from the root נס, like the meaning of 'raising a hand.'" "<b>Nedavat yadekha.</b> For burnt offering and peace offerings."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Reading הנו״ן as 'the nun' (the quiescent root letter nun), resolved by context of the dagesh in samekh indicating assimilation."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:41.149395427Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}